### Fitting MG94 with double instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -4566.09, AIC-c =  9261.63 (64 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0754
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.4033
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.035               |    44.741     |                                   |
|               0.716               |    36.477     |                                   |
|               3.850               |    18.783     |                                   |


### Fitting MG94 with double and triple instantaneous substitutions
* Log(L) = -4564.44, AIC-c =  9260.36 (65 estimated parameters)
* non-synonymous/synonymous rate ratio =   0.0763
* rate at which 2 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.3109
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon =   0.4128
* rate at which 3 nucleotides are changed instantly within a single codon between synonymous codon islands =   0.4128
* The following relative rate distribution (mean 1) for site-to-site **non-synonymous** rate variation was inferred

|               Rate                | Proportion, % |               Notes               |
|-----------------------------------|---------------|-----------------------------------|
|               0.000               |    37.781     |                                   |
|               0.616               |    42.755     |                                   |
|               3.784               |    19.464     |                                   |


